th between fights  you're less likely to die because you  ran out of healing items and more likely  to die because you misjudged a combat  situation if that makes sense so to  match my theory of taking more damage  during fights and getting more healing  between them it sort of matches up with  what we've seen from the gameplay since  there's this big focus on AI and  tackling enemy interaction in a clever  and really skillful way in his  experience with the game Rubicon noted  that the combat felt heavy and intense  like every blow mattered and if you  [ __ ] up if you were hit it was really  hard to recover especially if there were  multiple enemies he also noticed that  there was a really a lot more chip  damage over time so like I said earlier  to match the new healing system it  sounds like mistakes will punish you  more and that you'll be taking a lot  more consistent damage you'll be more  likely to die in the short term because  of a serious combat mistake or a series  of combat mistakes rather than die in  the long term because you kept chugging  Estus and kept tanking hits until you  ran out of healing items so you're less  likely to die than like that in the long  term so anyway click here for part two  where I go on to talk about the new  classes like the duel swordsman how  dodging and back stabs are no longer the  same  now the torch no longer blocks 100%  physical damage and oh also how there's  no games for Windows Live logo on the  website  oh yeah and leave a like if you enjoyed  this video cheers guys I'll see you next  time
 

